WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
A smaller total can hide a higher daily rate. Compare the day counts before the totals. Fictional entries in CAD; no health or quitting outcome is implied.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
Earlier: CAD 84 divided by 28 days is CAD 3 per day. Later: CAD 56 divided by 14 days is CAD 4 per day. Both records use the same currency.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.000
The later total is smaller, but its daily average is CAD 1 higher. Different-length periods can reverse a totals-only comparison.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
Use your own totals and day counts in this separate free browser companion. A spending difference does not explain its cause. Optional CraveBreaker iPhone app linked on the page. Published by Honest Little Apps.
